Optional switch-off of the Verilator commit trace (BP55 harness).

Under Verilator, core/cva6.sv writes one line per committed instruction to
trace_hart_<id>.dasm in the working directory. For the 21 benchmark programs
that is about 30 bytes x 295 M instructions per variant (several GB), and
parallel runs started from the same directory all write the same file. With
+define+BP55_NO_DASM_TRACE (set by cva6/cva6.sh) the mock tracer is not
compiled; without the define the file is unchanged.

diff --git a/core/cva6.sv b/core/cva6.sv
index 5b7c505..e13e2b8 100644
--- a/core/cva6.sv
+++ b/core/cva6.sv
@@ -1857,6 +1857,8 @@ module cva6
   );
 
   // mock tracer for Verilator, to be used with spike-dasm
+`elsif BP55_NO_DASM_TRACE
+  // (BP55 harness: no per-instruction trace file)
 `else
 
   int f;
